<ArticleLayout slug="google-merchant-center-image-requirements" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p>Reviewed October 23, 2026. By <a href="/about/team/cyril-drouin">Cyril Drouin</a>.</p>

  <p class="standfirst">Merchant Center checks the picture and the file behind its URL. The image attribute determines which rules apply. Today’s minimum and the coming minimum are different, and AI metadata must survive the export.</p>

  <h2>What are the Google Shopping image requirements?</h2>

  <p>Google Shopping image requirements cover the pictured product, file size, and crawlable URL. Prepare main images at Google’s recommended 1500 x 1500 pixels or above, keep AI metadata, and check the dated minimums below. Lifestyle images have their own rules. hubStudio supplies image creation and export; you submit the URLs through your Merchant Center data source.</p>

  <h3>Main image: image_link</h3>

