  <blockquote class="evidence">Google allows up to 10 additional images and recommends 1500 x 1500 pixels or above. Method: read the attribute’s format table, notice, and exceptions together, including its rule for undersized additional images.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Google Merchant Center Help, Additional image link, undated, accessed October 23, 2026. https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324370?hl=en</p>

  <p>An additional image below the minimum won’t be shown, but it does not itself disapprove the product. That exception is about size, not permission to add promotional overlays.</p>

  <h2>How does lifestyle_image_link differ?</h2>

  <p>This optional attribute supplies a scene for free listings: the product in use, staged in a room, or shown as part of a set. It is not a replacement for the required main image.</p>

